agonal direction  on the controller  you can sometimes prevent a ring out  from even happening  what about those edges that have walls  or barriers then well it's not too much  fun being up against these either  being stuck against the wall your  backwards movement is very restricted  and makes it much harder to play good  defense like ring outs being proactive  and trying to avoid the situation before  it even happens  is best if you get hit into a wall  instead of a ring out you'll get hit by  a wall splat  your back will hit the wall and you'll  slide down slowly completely vulnerable  to more attack  in fact you can wall splat twice in the  same combo leading to some damaging  sequences  and even more than that some walls are  breakable barricades that will shatter  when you wasp that into them this  transforms the stage revealing a new way  to ring out your opponent  making it especially dangerous both ring  outs and walls lead to huge damage in  soul calibur 6.  you can prevent this by moving around  the arena that way you don't get stuck  near the edge  and if you do get stuck just be really  patient with your defense you know you  can try to slowly inch away after  blocking the attack and to try to get  away from the edge or the wall you can  also surprise your opponent by using one  of your special attack that flips them  over your back instead  that's it for this episode this tutorial  is made in partnership with the  playstation competition center team  you can sign up for open series  competitions on compete.playstation.com  subscribe to the bne esports channel for  more tutorials  and soul calibur 6 content

